  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NAB&apos;IL: Organized Mayan and Mestizo Youth Contributing to the Construction of Inclusive Societies and Peaceful Coexistence in Huehuetenango</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to promote the creation of new models for the safe participation and protection of Mayan and Mestizo youth in San Pedro Necta and Cuilco Huehuetenango, Guatemala, so that they can be included in community and municipal government spaces from which they can contribute to strengthen social cohesion, the exercise of democracy and their rights, consolidate peace in the territory and promote psychosocial well-being. The project will be developed in partnership with youth organizations, the diaspora, municipal, community and ancestral authorities and the private sector, with the aim of creating an inclusive, safe and enabling environment for meaningful participation and the full exercise of human rights, with emphasis on young women and indigenous population.</narrative>
  </description>
